# 🖥️ GUI vs CLI & 🌐 Traffic Analysis (Cisco Packet Tracer)

## 📅 What I Learned Today
Today I learned the difference between **GUI** and **CLI**, and how to perform **traffic analysis using Cisco Packet Tracer**.  
These are core networking fundamentals every network engineer must understand.

---

## 🖱️ GUI (Graphical User Interface)

**Definition:**  
A visual interface that allows users to interact with systems using icons, menus, and buttons.

### 🔹 Features
- Easy to use  
- Mouse-based navigation  
- Beginner friendly  
- Slower for advanced configuration  

### 🔹 Example in Networking
In **Cisco Packet Tracer**, routers and switches can be configured visually using the GUI by clicking and setting parameters.

### 🔹 When to Use
- Learning networking basics  
- Small configurations  
- Visualizing network topology  

---

## 💻 CLI (Command Line Interface)

**Definition:**  
A text-based interface where users type commands to configure and manage devices.

### 🔹 Features
- Faster and more powerful  
- Used by professionals  
- Requires command knowledge  
- Full control over devices  

### 🔹 Basic Cisco Commands
```bash
enable
configure terminal
interface fastethernet 0/1
ip address 192.168.1.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
